# Unsplash Wallpapers App Implementation Plan

This document outlines the architecture and steps to build the Unsplash Wallpapers App using Flutter, Riverpod, Clean Architecture, and the Unsplash API.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Please review the proposed architecture, dependencies, and provide feedback on the open questions below before execution begins.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> 1. **Unsplash API Key**: To consume the Unsplash API, an Access Key is required. Are you able to provide this key, or should I create a `.env` file template where you can insert it yourself later? I propose adding `flutter_dotenv` to securely manage this key.
> 2. **Masonry Grid Layout**: Wallpapers usually have varying aspect ratios. Do you approve of adding the `flutter_staggered_grid_view` package to create a beautiful Pinterest-like Masonry Grid, or would you prefer a standard, uniform GridView?
> 3. **Offline Mode Details**: Currently, the app shows an offline screen if there is no connection. Would you like to use local caching (e.g., SQLite or Hive) to save previously loaded images for offline viewing, or is it sufficient to just show an error/offline screen while disconnected? (Given the constraints, I will start with an offline screen and caching images via `cached_network_image`).

## Proposed Architecture (Clean Architecture)

We will structure the `lib/` directory as follows:

```text
lib/
├── core/
│   ├── network/          # Network connectivity (existing)
│   ├── config/           # Theme, Constants, Environment variables
│   └── error/            # Custom exceptions and failures
├── data/
│   ├── datasources/      # Unsplash API calls using Dio
│   ├── models/           # JSON serializable models
│   └── repositories/     # Implementation of domain repository interfaces
├── domain/
│   ├── entities/         # Core business objects (e.g., Wallpaper)
│   └── repositories/     # Repository interfaces
└── presentation/
    ├── providers/        # Riverpod State Notifiers and Providers
    ├── screens/          # UI Screens (Home, Search, Details)
    └── widgets/          # Reusable UI components (WallpaperCard, etc.)
```

## Proposed Changes

