Provider using `shared_preferences` to persist Dark/Light mode selection.
#### [NEW] lib/domain/entities/wallpaper.dart
Entity representing a wallpaper image.
#### [NEW] lib/domain/repositories/wallpaper_repository.dart
Interface for searching and fetching wallpapers.

### Data Layer
#### [NEW] lib/data/models/wallpaper_model.dart
Data model with `fromJson` to parse Unsplash API responses.
#### [NEW] lib/data/datasources/unsplash_remote_data_source.dart
Dio client configured to call `https://api.unsplash.com/search/photos` and `https://api.unsplash.com/photos`.
#### [NEW] lib/data/repositories/wallpaper_repository_impl.dart
Implementation of the domain repository, handling exceptions.

### Presentation Layer
#### [NEW] lib/presentation/providers/wallpaper_provider.dart
Riverpod `StateNotifier` to handle loading, success, error states, and **infinite pagination (Lazy Loading)**.
#### [NEW] lib/presentation/providers/theme_provider.dart
Manages the current theme mode (Dark/Light).
#### [MODIFY] lib/presentation/screens/home_screen.dart
Implement a Search bar, Theme toggle button, and a Grid of wallpapers using lazy loading.
#### [NEW] lib/presentation/widgets/wallpaper_grid.dart
Component to render the list/grid of wallpapers and a loading indicator at the bottom for pagination.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- N/A for this phase, but we can add unit tests for the data layer parsing if needed.

### Manual Verification
1. Launch the app and verify it connects to the Unsplash API and loads initial images.
2. Search for a specific keyword (e.g., "Nature") and verify the results update.
3. Scroll to the bottom of the list and verify new images load automatically (Pagination).
4. Toggle the Dark/Light mode and verify the UI updates and the choice persists after restarting the app.
5. Turn off the internet connection and verify the "Offline Mode" UI is displayed correctly.
